edium", "notes": ["Incumbent Darline Graham (R) is running."]}, "overview": "South Carolina's Senate race is closer than the state's Republican lean would normally suggest. Incumbent Darline Graham faces Democrat Annie Andrews, who has outraised the incumbent by a wide margin, though outside spending has flowed heavily to Graham. Late-October polls from both parties' pollsters show the race within a few points, and Washington Post and AP coverage describes the seat as at risk of slipping to Democrats.\n\nStill, every major race rater calls the contest Lean or Likely Republican, and prediction markets give Andrews only about a one-in-five chance. Trump's last-minute rally in a deep-red state underscores Republican anxiety but also the structural advantage Graham retains. The forecast expects Graham to win by a modest margin, with meaningful uncertainty given the thin and partisan polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1565, "margin": -5.15}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2122, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2115, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2143, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1474, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2135, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2708, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2623, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2878, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2627, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2896, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2599, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2566, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.194, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1953, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2084, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.1997, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2291, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.2418, "margin": -3.5}, {"